TITLE:: ProtationWord
SUMMARY:: Mechanical words and circle-partition coding
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pqmc, Classes/PnumSeq, Classes/Pseries

DESCRIPTION::
Normalizes alpha and phase modulo one. With nil cuts, yields the lower mechanical binary word floor((n+1)*alpha+phase) - floor(n*alpha+phase), indexed from zero. With cuts, evaluates (n*alpha+phase) modulo one and returns its zero-based interval index; an exact cut belongs to the interval to its right. Rational rotations are periodic in exact arithmetic; an irrational binary mechanical coding is Sturmian in exact arithmetic. Finite precision limits both statements in software. Direct formula evaluation avoids cumulative phase-addition drift. Indices above 2147483646 are guarded. Storage is constant plus the cuts; partition evaluation is O(cuts.size).

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: alpha
Finite number, Function or Pattern sampled once, normalized modulo one.
ARGUMENT:: phase
Finite number, default 0; sampled once and normalized modulo one.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: cuts
Nil for mechanical binary coding, or a literal strictly increasing collection in (0,1). Empty cuts gives the constant interval index 0.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
ProtationWord((5.sqrt - 1) / 2, length: 16).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: ProtationWord / Value stream
var values = {
ProtationWord((5.sqrt - 1) / 2, length: 16).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: if(x.isArray) { x*7 } { x*7 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.07)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical mapping
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \mallet, \degree, ProtationWord((5.sqrt - 1) / 2, length: 32).collect { |x| [0, 7][x] }, \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Balanced binary rhythm
code::
ProtationWord((5.sqrt - 1) / 2, length: 24).collect { |x| [Rest(0.125), 0.125][x] }.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: ProtationWord / Balanced binary rhythm
var values = {
ProtationWord((5.sqrt - 1) / 2, length: 24).collect { |x| [Rest(0.125), 0.125][x] }.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: 0, dur: x, amp: 0.1)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Complementary streams
code::
ProtationWord(2.sqrt - 1, length: 16).collect { |x| [x, 1-x] }.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: ProtationWord / Complementary streams
var values = {
ProtationWord(2.sqrt - 1, length: 16).collect { |x| [x, 1-x] }.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: [0,7], amp: x*0.09, dur: 0.2)
}.play;
)
::

